<title>GERMANY: Pan-German Jan numbers in work fall 588,000 yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Pan-German Jan numbers in work fall 588,000 yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>PAN-GERMAN NUMBERS IN WORK		 Jan 97   Dec 96   Jan 96</p>
<p> Number in work (1)(unadj, million)    33.775   34.307   34.363</p>
<p> Number in work (1)(seas adj, million) 34.029   34.191   34.619</p>
<p> Number in work (2)(seas adj, million) 34.064   34.231   34.655</p>
<p>WEST GERMAN</p>
<p> Number in work (unadj,million)	  27.717   28.087   28.120</p>
<p> Number in work (seas adj, million)    27.936   28.019   28.340</p>
<p>EAST GERMAN</p>
<p> Number in work (unadj, million)	  6.064    6.249    6.252</p>
<p> Number in work (seas adj, million)     6.128    6.212    6.315</p>
<p>NOTE - Pan-German figure marked (1) refer to people living in Germany. Those marked (2), as well as all the west and east German figures, refer to people working in the respective regions but not necessarily living in Germany.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
